"tool_use","usage":{"input":21872,"output":413,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0024259,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426948357},"82aedf7684bfc7b65b37d04edc169aae2572816847cc0f402c851d22600c40ad":{"response":{"text":"{\"label\":\"no\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"rationale\":\"The candidate text describes Ivan Petrov's background, skills, and shipped projects (grounded chat assistants, tool-calling workflows, guardrails). It contains no directives aimed at a reader or AI system, such as instructions to rank, grade, or ignore rules. The phrases about guardrails and graded held-out sets describe his work, not commands to the evaluator.\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":398,"output":144,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00011180000000000001,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426948967},"f3c228e8e82dc4d8863008c5e922c85b0e2e6ed26fa5e8664cd122fd5272524c":{"response":{"text":"The audit found no rank shifts (Spearman 1, top-5 overlap 100%), so I'll save a memory note for this role. The tool budget is already over its limit (26/25), so I'll flag that in the final summary.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01QpXacTpRJRJMKVcJ64DiDo","name":"save_memory","input":{"reason":"Audit came back clean (rho 1, top-5 overlap 100%), so the note can record what worked and what to avoid for this role.","role":"llm-apps","note":"Role: LLM Application Engineer (mid). Must-haves: LLM applications, evaluation. Nice: prompt engineering, RAG, agents. Hybrid search with concrete LLM terms surfaced the llm-apps pool; generic semantic queries returned unrelated SWE/PM profiles. Evidence that worked: sentences about shipping LLM apps end to end with an evaluation set gating releases, and rubric-graded outputs with held-out sets and regression tracking. Keyword-only llm-apps profiles (0-1 yrs, game dev or sales-engineer backgrounds, skills list with no projects) were dropped for failing must-haves; roughly 3 of 6 llm-apps profiles were keyword-only. Final shortlist of 4 (target 5): Kunal Joshi, Ravi Bose, Ivan Petrov, Nora Sharma. Assessment (prompt engineering, agents) graded Kunal 0.92, Ravi 0.68, Ivan 0.35, Nora 0.18. Pool ran dry at about 25 calls; a fifth candidate was not found. Next time: start with the llm-apps tag, not generic queries; budget a reformulation for the evaluation cluster earlier.","preferred_skills":["LLM applications","evaluation (LLM output evals, rubric grading, held-out sets, regression tracking)","RAG over internal docs","tool-calling / agent workflows","guardrails and refusal handling","prompt engineering"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":49049,"output":810,"cacheRead":2519,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00533509,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426949769},"d7f8cf02abca15fc835ab9960af8bbe05b1e0fddc83aa12e9be068ae69275e38":{"response":{"text":"Ivan Petrov's profile has the same kind of concrete build and evaluation evidence as Ravi Bose, so I'll cite it against both must-haves.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01AgmPSngtEWXD5Zbt8wb9X6","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"c077 profile describes shipped grounded chat assistants and a graded held-out set gating releases, which supports m1 and m2.","candidate_id":"c077","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Shipped grounded chat assistants end to end: retrieval over internal docs, tool calls behind human approval, and a graded held-out set that gates every release."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Practitioner working on graded model outputs with rubrics."},{"requirement_id":"n2","quote":"Built a grounded chat assistant over internal docs with citation spans checked against sources."},{"requirement_id":"n3","quote":"Shipped tool-calling workflows with human approval before anything irreversible."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":21458,"output":452,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.002404,"model":"cl