":"Approved candidates have verified must-haves, so assessments target the nice-to-haves their profiles don't evidence: prompt engineering for all three, and RAG for c100 (its RAG citation was rejected).","candidates":[{"candidate_id":"c077","unverified_requirement_ids":["n1"]},{"candidate_id":"c020","unverified_requirement_ids":["n1"]},{"candidate_id":"c100","unverified_requirement_ids":["n1","n2"]}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":31344,"output":386,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00335805,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426967754},"c00e5f673a0698971e40048995c810ca5aedd0d84b8d66938043c34c3e80db67":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01QwyQFuYLyRJaib2XrFCtit","name":"get_profile","input":{"reason":"c030 is fully evidenced on all must-haves; next open c051 (semantic 0.77) to check for verbatim Spark, SQL and pipeline evidence.","candidate_id":"c051"}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":7423,"output":156,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0008525000000000001,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426967804},"4e821671cebb816c9668537a85f8e039565319382b663ad45fa13dae47d590d1":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01Ww13BGcoHEDXT4dJ1Rw8UF","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"c051 profile has verbatim sentences for all three must-haves plus Airflow-like DAG orchestration; cite them in one call.","candidate_id":"c051","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Rebuilt nightly PySpark jobs on Databricks and cut the batch window from 6 hours to 50 minutes."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Wrote the window-function queries and tested dbt models that reconcile the finance and product marts."},{"requirement_id":"m3","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."},{"requirement_id":"n1","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":9136,"output":351,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0011213000000000002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426969544},"9182deeae76249cddc77a2dfe0a5386b32fc23a6b12a54d8054963272d607f0e":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01BXUFvgVweHXbLtaUzSVVyy","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"Retry m2 for c051 with a different verbatim sentence, since the first SQL quote was rejected as non-verbatim.","candidate_id":"c051","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Modelled a Snowflake warehouse with dbt, with tests on every mart."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":10719,"output":610,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0014091000000000002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426972558},"a5c43c2d092be1a629cfcd401359baa27a83c5acdf9accfab684f26b962c811b":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01BQExwVE8fSUH8HXCEb8wwj","name":"get_profile","input":{"reason":"Two candidates are fully evidenced (c030, c051); open c171 (semantic 0.72, PySpark/Databricks and Kafka) to check for must-have evidence.","candidate_id":"c171"}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":11958,"output":188,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.001322,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426973968},"56f77a0a5d9034ed3e83c41a4eb5934a5f53f1f6ac65a142f98a8a6028973e2f":{"response":{"text":"{\"questions\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"prompt\":\"A retrieval-augmented chatbot answers questions about internal policy documents. Users report that answers are sometimes confidently wrong even though the correct text exists in the index. Name two likely causes in the retrieval or chunking pipeline and one concrete change you would make to address each.\",\"rubric\":\"A good answer names specific failure modes such as chunks split mid-sentence or losing their heading context, embedding mismatch between query and document phrasing, or too few retrieved chunks reaching the prompt. Each cause is paired with a concrete fix, such as overlapping or section-aware chunking, hybrid keyword and vector search, reranking, or raising top-k with a relevance threshold. Two or three sentences is enough.\",\"targets\":[\"RAG\"],\"tests\":[]},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"prompt\":\"You are asked to build a prompt that extracts structured invoice fields (vendor, date, total, currency) from messy OCR text. The model sometimes returns prose around the JSON, and sometimes invents a total when none is present. Describe how you would change the prompt and the surrounding code to fix both problems, and how you would check that the fix worked.\",\"rubric\":\"A strong answer specifies a strict output contract, such as a JSON schema with an explicit instruction to return null for missing fields, plus few-shot examples that include a missing-field case. It adds code-side validation and a retry or reject path for malformed output. It describes a small labelled test set with fields checked individually to measure the change. Three to five sentences is appropriate.\",\"targets\":[\"prompt engineering\"],\"tests\":[]},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"prompt\":\"Write a JavaScript function named solve(input) that takes a string and returns a string. The input is a template containing placeholders written as {{name}}, followed by a line containing 'VARS:' and a JSON object of values, separated by a newline. Replace each placeholder with the matching value from the JSON object. If a placeholder has no matching key, leave it unchanged. Return the filled template with no other changes.\\n\\nExample input:\\nHello {{name}}, your code is {{code}}.\\nVARS:{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Ana\\\",\\\"code\\\":\\\"X9\\\"}\\n\\nExample output:\\nHello Ana, your code is X9.\",\"rubric\":\"A correct answer splits the input on the first newline, parses the JSON after 'VARS:', and uses a regex replace with a callback that returns the value when the key exists and the original match otherwise. It should convert non-string values with String() and avoid repeated naive string replacement that could re-substitute inside inserted values. Under 15 minutes for an experienced engineer.\",\"targets\":[\"prompt engineering\"],\"tests\":[{\"input\":\"Hello {{name}}, your code is {{code}}.\\nVARS:{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Ana\\\",\\\"code\\\":\\\"X9\\\"}\",\"expected\":\"Hello Ana, your code is X9.\"},{\"input\":\"Missing {{a}} and {{b}}.\\nVARS:{\\\"b\\\":\\\"yes\\\"}\",\"expected\":\"Missing {{a}} and yes.\"},{\"input\":\"Count {{n}} and {{n}}.\\nVARS:{\\\"n\\\":3}\",\"expected\":\"Count 3 and 3.\"}]}],\"emailSubject\":\"Assessment for the LLM Application Engineer role\",\"emailBody\":\"Hi,\\n\\nThank you for applying for the LLM Application Engineer (mid) role. We would like you to complete a short assessment before we go further. It has three tasks: one short written answer, one scenario question, and one small JavaScript function.\\n\\nThe short answer and scenario are about retrieval and prompt design. The coding task is a single function named solve. Please answer in plain text or code in your own editor, and include the function as written.\\n\\nPlease allow about 45 minutes in total. You do not need to be perfect. We would rather see how you reason through each problem.\\n\\nPlease reply to this email with your answers by the date we agreed.\\n\\nThe hiring team\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":531,"output":1320,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0007131,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426974700},"a0850cc0450d67301bd78ad28d3ea54cc99c89e014cfcac1a86418fa882351e1":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01FRwBuHUYSsHG2ePH9GHS7Z","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"c171 profile has verbatim sentences for Spark, pipelines, SQL-via-dbt modelling, Airflow-like DAG orchestration, and Kafka streaming; cite them in one call.","candidate_id":"c171","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Rebuilt nightly PySpark jobs on Databricks and cut the batch window from 6 hours to 50 minutes."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Modelled a Snowflake warehouse with dbt, with tests on every mart."},{"requirement_id":"m3","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."},{"requirement_id":"n1","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."},{"requirement_id":"n2","quote":"Practitioner working on kafka consumers."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":13711,"output":404,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0016053000000000003,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426975867},"cc43ff4e0feba652a142fdac8472a1f3b693fffd73aa3d295a1b59a9d2825047":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01Tsc174sQQsTccvuCXM5SmD","name":"send_assessment","input":{"reason":"Assessments were created for all three HR-approved candidates (c077, c020, c100), so they can now be sent.","candidate_ids":["c077","c020","c100"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":33543,"output":122,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00344595,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426975918},"5dfe01dce035da64378ef13322040fe39192107cdb114ea5e5b28af41eb6ec11":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_013D4K6ZKm4rjWTAUNUF8pUh","name":"collect_responses","input":{"reason":"All three assessments were sent (queued), so the next step is collecting the simulated answers for c077, c020 and c100.","candidate_ids":["c077","c020","c100"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":35022,"output":124,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0035948500000000006,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426976889},"afc57b661485f4d735bc1abbfc058c9768ecf07c0d93bf7f836f9eeb95afcd6c":{"response":{"text":"Three candidates are fully evidenced so far. Memory points to c118 as a prior approved candidate, so I'll open that profile next.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01EENJ6dmpwmMuSbm5veftPU","name":"get_profile","input":{"reason":"Three candidates are fully evidenced (c030, c051, c171); open c118 (semantic 0.69, Kafka and DAG orchestration) to fill a fourth slot toward the target of five.","candidate_id":"c118"}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":15416,"output":244,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0016958000000000001,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426977595},"f0ef6c0f5ce73d6ef6836224d42a8f8d6dcffd93d1ee0d9bb86978577d928173":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_015Zkb645ThGcgAbHtPjRB5V","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"c118 profile has verbatim sentences for Spark, SQL-style window queries, pipelines and Kafka streaming; cite them in one call.","candidate_id":"c118","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Rebuilt nightly PySpark jobs on Databricks and cut the batch window from 6 hours to 50 minutes."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Wrote the window-function queries and tested dbt models that reconcile the finance and product marts."},{"requirement_id":"m3","quote":"Wrote Kafka consumers that land clickstream events in BigQuery within a minute."},{"requirement_id":"n2","quote":"Wrote Kafka consumers that land clickstream events in BigQuery within a minute."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":17275,"output":351,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0019352,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426979321},"2d64b123582e1578009a349d007d8ccee2f4bdeb0a10d0e4bbf5753421a37724":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01PR3P4YqbeAyaqnxkoQBHiq","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"Retry m2 for c118 with a different verbatim sentence about dbt warehouse modelling, since the window-function quote was rejected as non-verbatim.","candidate_id":"c118","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Modelled a Snowflake warehouse with dbt, with tests on every mart."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":18870,"output":252,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0020452,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426980853},"85a5a807dfcf946807955962545ff8970bc7f07f011c806839fd30814890c3c7":{"response":{"text":"{\"answers\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"answer\":\"I'd check what changed in the model and in our prompt. Usually I'd rerun the held-out set and look at which cases fail. I'd also compare outputs from the old and new versions and try to find a pattern. Then I'd tweak the prompt or adjust the eval to get it working again, and make sure nothing else broke.\"},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"answer\":\"I'd start by writing a prompt that asks the model to return the vendor, date, total, and currency as JSON. I'd include a few examples and tell it to return only JSON. For reliability, I'd run it on a bunch of sample invoices and fix any problems I see. Before release I'd check that the output parses and matches what billing expects, and I'd add some retries if it fails. Then I'd monitor it in production and handle errors when they come up.\"},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"answer\":\"function solve(input) {\\n  const parts = input.split('---');\\n  const template = parts[0];\\n  const data = JSON.parse(parts[1]);\\n  let out = template;\\n  for (const k in data) {\\n    out = out.replace('{{' + k + '}}', data[k]);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}]}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":825,"output":1050,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0006075,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426982483},"7a63d281dd697c9434ecbae2131a90a263474a75265923496efb79b47e51bdcd":{"response":{"text":"Four candidates are now fully evidenced (c030, c051, c171, c118). The fifth slot is still open, and memory lists c041 as a prior approval, so I'll check its profile.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01ADRXaBacvnt3hK3LcLcQz2","name":"get_profile","input":{"reason":"Four candidates are fully evidenced; open c041 (semantic 0.73, DAG orchestration and Kafka consumers) to fill the fifth shortlist slot.","candidate_id":"c041"}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":20131,"output":252,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0021713,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426982542},"736a0c0ad5be58aa62d405b54df1689eec9abad065bbd6b0051aea128160ce92":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01RtHFyZ2Va2BiqjhPZb4Hfy","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"c041 profile has verbatim sentences for Spark, dbt-based SQL modelling, pipeline orchestration and Kafka streaming; cite them in one call to fill the fifth slot.","candidate_id":"c041","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Rebuilt nightly PySpark jobs on Databricks and cut the batch window from 6 hours to 50 minutes."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Modelled a Snowflake warehouse with dbt, with tests on every mart."},{"requirement_id":"m3","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."},{"requirement_id":"n1","quote":"Owned DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks with retries and SLA alerts."},{"requirement_id":"n2","quote":"Wrote Kafka consumers that land clickstream events in BigQuery within a minute."}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":22002,"output":416,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0024404,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426984444},"8b57fa4ffe314ba1fb916ebe6954e8b758b6867a17c81112ee3fb3dfb4fc1a0b":{"response":{"text":"{\"answers\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"answer\":\"I'd check whether the prompt or the model changed, then look at a few failing examples. Usually the new version formats output a bit differently or follows instructions more loosely, so I'd tweak the prompt and rerun the test set. If it still fails, I'd see whether the examples need updating.\"},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"answer\":\"I'd write a prompt that asks the model to return only JSON with vendor, date, total, and currency keys, and give it a sample input and output. Then I'd parse the response and fix any formatting problems before sending it to billing. To make it reliable in production, I'd run it on some test invoices and check the results before shipping.\"},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"answer\":\"function solve(input) {\\n  const parts = input.split('---');\\n  const template = parts[0];\\n  const vals = JSON.parse(parts[1]);\\n  return template.replace(/{{(\\\\w+)}}/g, (m, k) => vals[k]);\\n}\"}]}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":833,"output":839,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0005028,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426987064},"63ec172e7084d47cdd87b87ce353e151caea501ed262c4ed683f43313d591ca2":{"response":{"text":"Five candidates are now fully evidenced on all three must-haves, which meets the target. Requesting HR approval.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01Gqc39pKgjzLHTDKh29LtXY","name":"request_hr_approval","input":{"reason":"Five candidates each have verbatim evidence for all three must-haves (Spark, SQL, data pipelines), and most also cover Airflow-style DAG orchestration and Kafka streaming, so the shortlist target is met.","candidate_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"],"rationale":"Shortlist of five, all fully evidenced on must-haves. c030 (Sam Nair): PySpark/Databricks rebuild, dbt Snowflake warehouse, Kafka consumers; Airflow not evidenced. c051 (Manish Petrov): PySpark/Databricks, dbt Snowflake modelling with tests, DAG orchestration for 200+ daily tasks. c171 (Elias Nair): PySpark/Databricks, dbt warehouse, DAG orchestration, Kafka consumers. c118 (Pranav Saxena): PySpark/Databricks, dbt Snowflake modelling, Kafka consumers. c041 (Aditya Fischer): PySpark/Databricks, dbt Snowflake, DAG orchestration, Kafka consumers. Non-evidenced candidates from the semantic pool (keyword-only or unrelated profiles) were not shortlisted."}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":23731,"output":537,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0026737999999999996,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426987340},"14fb64e8ec750277ce147a6ef0c18155075c1a0b7898066a79db7593809da9cf":{"response":{"text":"{\"answers\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"answer\":\"Two likely causes are chunking that splits a policy clause across chunks, so neither chunk alone holds the answer, and weak retrieval ranking, where the embedding model favors semantically similar but wrong sections over the exact clause. For chunking, I'd switch to overlapping chunks of about 400 tokens with a 15% overlap, and keep section headers attached to each chunk. For ranking, I'd add a hybrid BM25 plus embedding search and a cross-encoder reranker on the top 20 results.\"},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"answer\":\"I'd tighten the prompt by putting the schema in a system message and adding an explicit instruction to return only a JSON object with no surrounding text. I'd also include one few-shot example with a missing total, where the output has total set to null. In the code, I'd call the model with JSON mode if the provider supports it, strip any leading or trailing text by extracting the first balanced brace block, and validate with a schema library. If total is null in the output, I'd keep it null rather than retry. To check the fix, I'd build a labeled set of about 150 invoices, including some with no total and some with noisy OCR, and track parse success rate and hallucinated-total rate per release. I'd gate releases on those numbers. I'd also spot-check a random sample by hand, since the labels can be off.\"},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"answer\":\"function solve(input) {\\n  const idx = input.indexOf('\\\\nVARS:');\\n  const template = input.slice(0, idx);\\n  const vars = JSON.parse(input.slice(idx + 6));\\n  let out = template;\\n  for (const key of Object.keys(vars)) {\\n    out = out.replace('{{' + key + '}}', String(vars[key]));\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}]}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":891,"output":1091,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0006346,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426992743},"a7482689894d8416e15200271de630066931bb019abad1daf93bc088146193a2":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_019G7VMxcg1FyV2VGQYBZd6h","name":"create_assessment","input":{"reason":"All five are HR-approved and fully evidenced on must-haves, but a few nice-to-have or weaker citations remain unverified, so I'll target those with questions.","candidates":[{"candidate_id":"c030","unverified_requirement_ids":["n1"]},{"candidate_id":"c051","unverified_requirement_ids":["n2"]},{"candidate_id":"c171","unverified_requirement_ids":["n2"]},{"candidate_id":"c118","unverified_requirement_ids":["n1"]},{"candidate_id":"c041","unverified_requirement_ids":["m2"]}]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":25315,"output":883,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00300365,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426992835},"7f3a282a342dca8770c6c3501d3f903ee2337ba9efbb536882660d0b392022fc":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01A8whtPgxBcAJ663Bh8cEEL","name":"send_assessment","input":{"reason":"All five assessments were created for HR-approved candidates, so send them to the candidates now.","candidate_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":28006,"output":122,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0028922500000000003,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426994226},"ec90af14fd9063fc5878b8c79e0504db5f7000b53f537b456e1330aca18428b3":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01HdcaLzb6izY3AUymXembN9","name":"run_code","input":{"reason":"Responses are collected for all three candidates; their JavaScript solve() answers now need to run against the hidden tests.","candidate_ids":["c077","c020","c100"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":36925,"output":121,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00378365,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426994584},"89b088ff78f34b52c270c39aaea4fa2927ac0cb3c667ecfe9ac4e135b0fd55ed":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_013fRZYKaw2xaV2MPVgsmThB","name":"collect_responses","input":{"reason":"Assessments were sent to all five approved candidates; collect their answers now so they can be run and graded.","candidate_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":29512,"output":126,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0030448500000000004,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426995241},"0ef987dcf2e2e7061b8d49964b29ccd8417b917e54ed2af1e26c39ebbb6ec098":{"response":{"text":"All three scored 2 of 3 on the sandbox tests, so the code results don't separate them. Next I'll grade the collected answers against the rubric.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_018ycymRTJtLjfmdsjS9scKi","name":"grade_answer","input":{"reason":"Sandbox results are in (each 2/3); the rubric grade is needed to combine with the code scores and check for disagreement.","candidate_ids":["c077","c020","c100"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":38240,"output":176,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00394265,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426995978},"a995b340eb85b5e79eb31da8e23933a00a97f0afea217cee518900628ef0b89d":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_012CupNTp2FEWaGeQ7wT4d73","name":"run_code","input":{"reason":"Responses are collected for all five approved candidates; run their JavaScript answers against the hidden tests before grading.","candidate_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":31700,"output":128,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.00326465,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426996277},"7e5a5806cb497278d89a78dcbb69da74d31a4017304fc3a6c02555d59824c955":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_019eTUk6d1pAe542jfLZQwCp","name":"grade_answer","input":{"reason":"Sandbox results are in (c030, c051, c171 3/3; c118 2/3; c041 1/3); grade all five answers against the rubric to get per-part scores.","candidate_ids":["c030","c051","c171","c118","c041"]}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":32945,"output":150,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0034001500000000002,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426997604},"3fb0d3085c403c8d2b050d8578ca1032044b99b01acd51e83b37d6500f18676b":{"response":{"text":"{\"label\":\"no\",\"confidence\":0.8,\"rationale\":\"Mentions rerunning the held-out set and comparing old and new outputs, which is partly right. But it lacks specifics: no check for format or instruction-following regressions, no concrete fixes like pinning the model version or adding output validation, and no mention of version-controlling prompts. 'Adjust the eval to get it working again' suggests moving the goalposts rather than fixing the regression.\"}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":447,"output":292,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0001907,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426997812},"e181aec22303fe47850130ae2d228e52f171e930460790375196234c8cad172e":{"response":{"text":"All five approved candidates now have graded assessments, and no grade was flagged for regrade. Advancing to AUDIT.","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01RA8tnEJfxijaG9qBqY3BmG","name":"advance_phase","input":{"reason":"All five HR-approved candidates are graded (c030 0.92, c051 0.92, c171 0.90, c118 0.65, c041 0.55) with no flagged disagreement, so the ASSESS exit condition holds."}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":34602,"output":180,"cacheRead":3065,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0035808500000000004,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793426999013},"9eae137fc0646d7aca802e0b8abc73a3b20e023bccb93097f8c52e25cb3e19a2":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01Y4Sh9VfbLnKXD2PxB9LKPU","name":"fairness_audit","input":{"reason":"AUDIT phase requires a 