atch; I need verbatim sentences for the must-haves."}}],"stopReason":"tool_use","usage":{"input":6054,"output":250,"cacheRead":3220,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0007626,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793428968651},"bff7c8461b88b56819c30ce0b28620eddb8df641b5b616d30a40c6d27df9223f":{"response":{"text":"{\"parts\":[{\"kind\":\"short\",\"score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.8,\"note\":\"Names model id and version per vector, batched idempotent backfill with progress tracking, and pinned query routing so results never mix models; it covers partial failure but says little explicitly about non-blocking reads.\"},{\"kind\":\"scenario\",\"score\":0.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"note\":\"Covers a durable queue, token-bucket rate limiting with batching, idempotent upserts on (document_id, model_version), dead-lettering with backoff, concrete lag metrics, and stuck-worker and poison-document failure modes; it does not name dimension mismatch.\"},{\"kind\":\"code\",\"score\":1.0,\"confidence\":0.95,\"note\":\"Correct step = k - o windowing with a break once the final token is reached, handles fewer tokens than k and empty input, uses no libraries, and passes all 3 hidden tests.\"}]}","toolUses":[],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":1646,"output":672,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"},"costUsd":0.0005006,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ts":1793428970303},"20189510ea16314f16c38d01d20754036e2c8f31cc080224c3affe44add793e9":{"response":{"text":"","toolUses":[{"id":"toolu_01QRqkHvNJ9s1VJfB9iqELX9","name":"cite_evidence","input":{"reason":"Kunal Joshi's profile has verbatim project sentences covering both must-haves plus RAG and agents, so I'm citing them in one call.","candidate_id":"c162","citations":[{"requirement_id":"m1","quote":"Built a grounded chat assistant over internal docs with citation spans checked against sources."},{"requirement_id":"m2","quote":"Graded model outputs with rubrics and a held-out set, and tracked regressions per rel